  <data name="txtExplanation.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Logical operators are used to combine or reverse Boolean conditions. They evaluate conditions and produce a Boolean result: True or False.

1. AND Operator

Returns True only when both conditions are True.

2. OR Operator

Returns True when at least one condition is True.

3. NOT Operator

Reverses a single value. Not True is False, and Not False is True.

4. XOR Operator

Returns True only when the two conditions are different.

HOW TO USE THE PROGRAM

1. Select a logical operator on the right.
2. Tick the A and B boxes (ticked = True, unticked = False).
3. Click SUBMIT to see the result. The matching row in the truth table is highlighted.
4. Click CLEAR to start over, or EXIT to close the program.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="txtSampleCode.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Dim A As Boolean = True
Dim B As Boolean = False

Dim andResult As Boolean = A And B   ' False
Dim orResult As Boolean = A Or B     ' True
Dim notResult As Boolean = Not A     ' False
Dim xorResult As Boolean = A Xor B   ' True

MessageBox.Show(
    "AND: " &amp; andResult &amp; vbCrLf &amp;
    "OR: " &amp; orResult &amp; vbCrLf &amp;
    "NOT A: " &amp; notResult &amp; vbCrLf &amp;
    "XOR: " &amp; xorResult)

' Using it in a decision:
If A And Not B Then
    MessageBox.Show("A is True and B is False")
End If</value>
  </data>
